WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.480
The web is something we
interact with every single day,

00:00:02.579 --> 00:00:05.920
but have you ever stopped to think about
what actually goes on behind the scenes?

00:00:05.969 --> 00:00:08.400
Imagine waking up in the
morning, grabbing your phone,

00:00:08.525 --> 00:00:10.080
and opening your favorite website.

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:13.280
Maybe it's YouTube, Instagram,
or your go-to news site.

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:16.960
It loads almost instantly, displaying all
the content right where you expect it.

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:18.010
But how does that happen?

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:20.240
What's making everything work so smoothly?

00:00:20.315 --> 00:00:23.360
Today, we're breaking it all
down in the simplest way possible,

00:00:23.510 --> 00:00:25.040
so that by the end of this video,

00:00:25.165 --> 00:00:27.680
you'll have a clear understanding
of what web development is

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:29.200
and how websites come to life.

00:00:29.350 --> 00:00:32.720
Web development is the process
of building and maintaining websites.

00:00:32.819 --> 00:00:34.640
It's what makes the internet function,

00:00:34.739 --> 00:00:37.360
from the way a page looks
to how it processes data,

00:00:37.509 --> 00:00:39.600
and responds to user interactions.

00:00:39.699 --> 00:00:41.200
Think of a website like a restaurant.

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:44.000
The front end is everything
you see as a customer.

00:00:44.124 --> 00:00:46.800
The menu, the tables, the ambience,

00:00:46.949 --> 00:00:48.400
the back end is like the kitchen,

00:00:48.499 --> 00:00:51.360
where chefs and staff work behind
the scenes to prepare your food

00:00:51.459 --> 00:00:53.680
and make sure everything
is running efficiently,

00:00:53.779 --> 00:00:55.520
and then we have
full stack development,

00:00:55.669 --> 00:00:57.520
which is like being the
owner of the restaurant

00:00:57.521 --> 00:01:00.800
who manages both the customer
experience and the kitchen operations.

00:01:00.949 --> 00:01:04.400
Front end development is all about
what users see and interact with.

00:01:04.449 --> 00:01:09.680
It involves three key technologies, HTML,
which structures the content of a web page,

00:01:09.779 --> 00:01:12.631
CSS, which styles it
with colors, fonts, and

00:01:12.731 --> 00:01:15.200
layouts, and JavaScript,
which makes it interactive.

00:01:15.349 --> 00:01:18.800
For example, when you hover
over a button and it changes color,

00:01:18.949 --> 00:01:20.480
that's JavaScript in action.

00:01:20.579 --> 00:01:23.760
The front end is crucial because
it affects the user experience.

00:01:23.909 --> 00:01:28.560
If a website is slow, hard to navigate or
looks outdated, users won't stick around.

00:01:28.709 --> 00:01:30.560
Next time you visit a site like Netflix,

00:01:30.561 --> 00:01:32.800
pay attention to how
smooth everything looks,

00:01:32.899 --> 00:01:34.960
the hover effects, the
scrolling animations,

00:01:34.961 --> 00:01:37.920
the clean layout, that's all
thanks to front end development.

00:01:38.069 --> 00:01:40.189
But what about everything
happening behind the scenes?

00:01:40.229 --> 00:01:42.160
That's where back end development comes in,

00:01:42.259 --> 00:01:44.640
the back end is responsible
for processing requests,

00:01:44.689 --> 00:01:47.920
storing and managing data, and
making sure everything works properly.

00:01:48.019 --> 00:01:50.000
When you log into Facebook, for example,

00:01:50.124 --> 00:01:53.040
the back end checks your username
and password against a database,

00:01:53.164 --> 00:01:55.760
retrieves your profile
information and loads your feed.

00:01:55.909 --> 00:01:58.320
It's the invisible engine that
keeps everything running.

00:01:58.369 --> 00:02:02.054
Back end development uses programming
languages like Python, PHP, Node.

00:02:02.079 --> 00:02:05.886
js, and frameworks
like Dejango, or Express.

00:02:05.986 --> 00:02:08.240
js to build the logic
behind a website.

00:02:08.390 --> 00:02:10.880
It also relies on databases
to store information,

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:13.200
such as user accounts, posts, and comments.

00:02:13.350 --> 00:02:14.880
Think of the back end like a brain.

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:18.880
It processes all the inputs and sends
back the right responses almost instantly.

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:22.000
Now, if someone knows how to build
both the front end and the back end,

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:24.000
they're called a full stack developer.

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:28.080
These developers can create entire websites
or applications from start to finish.

00:02:28.230 --> 00:02:30.000
They understand how
both parts work together

00:02:30.125 --> 00:02:32.199
and can switch between
designing a user-friendly

00:02:32.249 --> 00:02:34.400
interface and coding
the logic that powers it.

00:02:34.550 --> 00:02:36.640
Full stack developers are highly valued,

00:02:36.740 --> 00:02:38.880
especially in startups
and small businesses,

00:02:38.955 --> 00:02:40.782
because they can handle
the entire development

00:02:40.783 --> 00:02:42.880
process without needing
separate specialists.

00:02:43.030 --> 00:02:44.880
Imagine a full stack developer like a chef

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:46.640
who not only cooks the food,

00:02:46.765 --> 00:02:49.280
but also designs the
restaurant and manages the staff.

00:02:49.430 --> 00:02:52.320
They ensure that everything
works seamlessly from start to finish.

00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:54.480
So how exactly does a website work?

00:02:54.580 --> 00:02:58.480
Let's say you type google.com
into your browser and press enter.

00:02:58.630 --> 00:03:00.880
Your browser sends a
request to Google Server,

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:04.000
which processes the request,
fetches the necessary data,

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:05.760
and sends it back to your device.

00:03:05.860 --> 00:03:09.760
Thus, your browser then takes this data
and displays it as the Google homepage.

00:03:09.885 --> 00:03:13.829
This process happens in milliseconds, and
it's the result of a combination of front

00:03:13.853 --> 00:03:16.012
end and back end
development working together.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:18.000
Think of it like ordering food online.

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:20.080
You browse the menu, place an order,

00:03:20.230 --> 00:03:22.720
and wait for the restaurant to
prepare and deliver your food.

00:03:22.770 --> 00:03:24.640
Website's function in the same way.

00:03:24.740 --> 00:03:27.093
You request information,
the server processes

00:03:27.168 --> 00:03:29.200
it, and the result is
displayed on your screen.

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:31.120
Now that you know what web development is,

00:03:31.270 --> 00:03:32.880
which part excites you the most?

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:35.920
Are you more into designing
beautiful and interactive websites,

00:03:36.070 --> 00:03:38.640
or do you love the idea of
working behind the scenes,

00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:41.600
managing data, and making
everything function smoothly?

00:03:41.750 --> 00:03:43.360
Drop a comment below and let me know.

00:03:43.510 --> 00:03:46.560
And if this video helped you understand
web development a little better,

00:03:46.710 --> 00:03:49.440
don't forget to like and subscribe
for more tech breakdowns.

00:03:49.441 --> 00:03:50.480
See you in the next one.